IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`
IMPORT `ei2-work-sharing-and-courses`

-- Tests of ei2-work-sharing-and-courses (ss 24 to 26). Expected values are written by hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a course measure, s 59(a)`       MEANS JUST `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training`
`an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` MEANS JUST `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support`
`an assistance services measure, s 59(c)` MEANS JUST `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
`a research measure, s 59(d)`     MEANS JUST `ei2 s 59(d) measure supporting research, innovation or partnerships`
`an unlisted measure`             MEANS JUST `ei2 an employment support measure not described in paragraphs 59(a) to (d)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
`no measure` MEANS NOTHING

§ `s 24(2) and (3) - work-sharing`

-- "(2) A special or general direction of the Commission approving or disapproving a work sharing agreement ... is not subject to review under section 112."
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the direction on a work sharing agreement is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Any other decision: s 24(2) says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the direction on a work sharing agreement is not subject to review under section 112` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "(3) ... a claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during a week when the claimant works in work-sharing employment."
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the week` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A week without work-sharing employment: the subsection does not deem anything; it does not say the claimant is not unemployed.
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the week` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Helpers on the kinds of measure (s 59(a) to (d))`

#ASSERT `ei2 s 59 the measure is of the kind` `a course measure, s 59(a)` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training`
#ASSERT NOT `ei2 s 59 the measure is of the kind` `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training`
#ASSERT NOT `ei2 s 59 the measure is of the kind` `no measure` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training`

-- "other than one referred to in paragraph 59(a) or (c)": there is a measure and it is neither (a) nor (c).
#ASSERT NOT `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `no measure` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
#ASSERT NOT `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `a course measure, s 59(a)` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
#ASSERT NOT `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `an assistance services measure, s 59(c)` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
#ASSERT `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
#ASSERT `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `a research measure, s 59(d)` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
#ASSERT `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `an unlisted measure` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`

§ `s 25(1)(a) - a referred course or program`

-- Attending, at own expense, no measure, no s 63 agreement, referred: unemployed and available during it.
#ASSERT `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` TRUE TRUE `no measure` FALSE TRUE
-- The same but the claimant has not been referred.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` TRUE TRUE `no measure` FALSE FALSE
-- Not attending a course at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` FALSE TRUE `no measure` FALSE TRUE
-- Not at the claimant's own expense, under a measure of paragraph 59(a), referred.
#ASSERT `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` TRUE FALSE `a course measure, s 59(a)` FALSE TRUE
-- Under a measure of paragraph 59(b) only: the course is not one of the three funding routes.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` TRUE FALSE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` FALSE TRUE
-- Under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63.
#ASSERT `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` TRUE FALSE `no measure` TRUE TRUE
-- Under none of the three routes.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` TRUE FALSE `no measure` FALSE TRUE

§ `s 25(1)(b) - a referred employment activity`

-- Assistance under a prescribed measure of paragraph 59(b), referred.
#ASSERT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` TRUE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Under a measure of 59(a): "other than one referred to in paragraph 59(a) or (c)" excludes it, even if prescribed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` TRUE `a course measure, s 59(a)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Under a measure of 59(c): excluded.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` TRUE `an assistance services measure, s 59(c)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Under a measure of 59(d): not excluded by 25(1)(b)(i).
#ASSERT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` TRUE `a research measure, s 59(d)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- A measure of 59(b) that is not prescribed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` TRUE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- No measure, but assistance under a prescribed measure that is the subject of a s 63 agreement.
#ASSERT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` TRUE `no measure` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Not referred.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` TRUE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Not participating.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` FALSE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 25(1) and (2)`

#ASSERT `s 25(1) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the period` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25(2) the decision about the referral is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(2) the decision about the referral is not subject to review under section 112` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 26 - benefits are not earnings`

-- Benefits paid while employed under a measure of paragraph 59(b): not earnings.
#ASSERT `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` TRUE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Under a measure of 59(a): not excluded (only 59(c) and (d) are).
#ASSERT `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` TRUE `a course measure, s 59(a)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Under a measure of 59(c): excluded from the rule, so the section says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` TRUE `an assistance services measure, s 59(c)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under a measure of 59(d): excluded.
#ASSERT `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` TRUE `a research measure, s 59(d)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A measure of 59(c) is excluded but the claimant is also employed under a measure that is the subject of a s 63 agreement.
#ASSERT `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` TRUE `an assistance services measure, s 59(c)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No measure and no s 63 agreement.
#ASSERT `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` TRUE `no measure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No benefits paid while so employed.
#ASSERT `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` FALSE `an opportunities measure, s 59(b)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
